  "id": "ego-depletion",
  "term": "ego depletion",
  "definition": "Ego depletion is the idea that using self-control or self-regulation on one task can temporarily reduce a person’s ability to regulate themselves well on a later task. It is based on the view that self-resources such as attention, willpower, and cognitive energy are limited and can be used up for a time.",
